      "page_number": 1,
      "text": "GOVERNMENT OF EXAMPLE STATE\nDEPARTMENT OF REVENUE\nNo. REV/2026/114 Dated: 10 March 2026\nPUBLIC NOTICE\nProperty Tax Relief Scheme, 2026\nNotice is hereby given that the State Government has introduced the Property Tax Relief Scheme, 2026 for owners of residential property in Example State."
    },
    {
      "page_number": 2,
      "text": "2. Eligibility\n2.1 An owner is eligible if the property is used only for residence.\n3. Documents Required\n3.1 The following documents must be attached to the application:\n(a) a self-attested copy of the property tax receipt;\n(b) proof of ownership, such as a sale deed;"
    },
    {
      "page_number": 3,
      "text": "4. Last Date and Time Limits\n4.1 Applications must be submitted on or before 30 April 2026.\n4.3 Before any site inspection, the owner shall be given seven (7) days' notice in writing."
    },
    {
      "page_number": 5,
      "text": "6. Appeal\n6.1 Any person aggrieved by a decision under this Scheme may file an appeal before the Deputy Commissioner (Revenue) within thirty (30) days of the decision.\n7. Contact\n7.1 For help, contact the Revenue Helpline at 1800-000-0000."
    }
  ],
